#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb6ce8cf-b22f-5b84-af3d-ab897274d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329594} {:answer/id #uuid "f9940d43-9fe4-5521-b22e-f21603bb7c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329595} {:answer/id #uuid "43525099-f7a5-5795-9865-fb028757b5de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329596} {:answer/id #uuid "96f03684-5013-5a9a-aafd-6c9fa4546707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329597} {:answer/id #uuid "861b252a-74fc-5f26-a6fd-485388cfb322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ce8cf-b22f-5b84-af3d-ab897274d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329594} :answer-field/id #uuid "54d7e4c2-b00e-5450-a3fb-08e3c871117f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ee0bbb6-7fc1-5766-b761-cf4d607ded40" :question/math-academy-id "q-20145" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,1,2)$, $B(3,3,3)$, $C(-2,-1,3)$, and $D(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+4k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)-2((-4)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)+((-4)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-4+20+4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|20|=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f51eeb-87d3-5f06-9404-e21666f85c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20f51eeb-87d3-5f06-9404-e21666f85c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329601} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6dc0cac-3e51-5c86-afe9-d37ced4615bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "46a75f72-6b10-51d9-969a-5bb2a80a1f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-280321" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,-3,2),$ $B(4,-1,5),$ $C(-2,0,1),$ and $D(3,-2,3).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j+5k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+3k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1)-2((-3)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-3)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(3+1)-2(-3+2)+3(-3-6) \\\\  & =12+2-27 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-13|=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aced0243-d92c-5ba8-b4e3-6ec5e2287249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329604} {:answer/id #uuid "81862d97-1216-5914-97d9-11cc9150e812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aced0243-d92c-5ba8-b4e3-6ec5e2287249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329604} :answer-field/id #uuid "57ddaa61-e3f0-5719-9b3c-6b9758166523" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75f2dcba-97e6-5847-805b-d61c763d8b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75f2dcba-97e6-5847-805b-d61c763d8b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329607} :answer-field/id #uuid "01b4a8fe-5411-5e14-8fb5-cb9cecfa0198" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7345efee-0837-55d4-aa30-71626bea7919" :question/math-academy-id "q-280735" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨4,{k}^{2},2⟩$, $b=⟨1,5,3⟩$, and $c=⟨2,1,0⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n**In ascending order:** $\\,$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}\n$\\,$\nand\n$\\,$\n$k=${{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & {k}^{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-{k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 1)-{k}^{2}(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 2)+2(1\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =4(-3)-{k}^{2}(0-6)+2(1-10) \\\\  & =-12+6{k}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =6{k}^{2}-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the triple product equal to 0:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{k}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 6{k}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =5 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if \n$k=-\\sqrt{5}$ or $k=\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "333e7ac2-5a7e-520b-8d9a-ae757a762a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "333e7ac2-5a7e-520b-8d9a-ae757a762a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329610} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab4282f0-49bf-56d9-82d0-91b23cd0b794" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d07bb59-9dba-5ceb-bfb0-c624285988a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-281023" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,2),$ $B(3,4,5),$ $C(6,2,4),$ and $D(5,3,6).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,4,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(6i+2j+4k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =5i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨5,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+3j+6k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =4i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨4,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3)-4(5\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 4)+3(5\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2(8-6)-4(20-8)+3(15-8) \\\\  & =4-48+21 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-23|=23.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0e3bd3a-e1ee-5601-8efa-f03f35533bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329613} {:answer/id #uuid "a43198df-65d3-5447-a7cf-4b55146ed6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329614} {:answer/id #uuid "a259c2b4-988f-525e-8bb1-f664ff7aa4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329615} {:answer/id #uuid "205a4d16-c6d0-51c0-b9a1-cf5bad6bfc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329616} {:answer/id #uuid "0617eae5-6788-5fdf-8ed9-547247f564e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0e3bd3a-e1ee-5601-8efa-f03f35533bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329613} :answer-field/id #uuid "319f1908-5c5d-53a9-aecb-7b022821be39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f365c4c0-98f0-554f-8b7b-fe99ef2088ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-73736" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,1,t⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and $r=⟨3,0,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & 1 & t \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1))-(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))+t(2\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-t-5+3t \\\\  & =2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 2t-5 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =5 \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=\\frac{5}{2}.$"}]}
